---
source: src/hooks/installer.rs
bead: bd-3usjw.7
surface: trauma_guard_hook_helper
assertion: ee hook preflight-shell --shell bash emits a deterministic, syntactically-valid advisory snippet that may surface ee preflight output but always allows the upcoming command
schema:
  envelope: ee.response.v2
  payload: ee.hooks.preflight_shell.v1
contracts:
  - snippet body is byte-identical across runs for the same (shell, ee_binary_path) pair
  - snippet embeds a single-quoted absolute ee binary path (no PATH lookup)
  - snippet does not enable extdebug, prompt on /dev/tty, return nonzero, or otherwise suppress shell execution
  - even `ee preflight check` exit code 7 is advisory and the hook returns success
  - inherited `set -e` cannot turn a nonzero advisory lookup into command suppression
  - candidate commands execute after advisory output is surfaced
  - version field is the first 16 hex chars of blake3(snippet) for upgrade detection
  - snippet does not embed a client-side severity blocklist
evidence:
  - src/hooks/installer.rs::generate_preflight_shell_snippet
  - src/hooks/installer.rs::bash_preflight_snippet
  - tests/preflight_hook_bash.rs::bash_snippet_syntax_check_passes
  - tests/preflight_hook_bash.rs::bash_snippet_source_defines_hook_function_and_activation_flag
  - tests/preflight_hook_bash.rs::bash_snippet_treats_preflight_exit_7_as_advisory
  - tests/preflight_hook_bash.rs::bash_debug_trap_allows_candidate_command_after_preflight_exit_7
  - tests/preflight_hook_bash.rs::bash_snippet_is_byte_stable_across_runs_for_pinned_binary_path
  - tests/preflight_hook_bash.rs::bash_snippet_carries_documented_contract_markers
